All 36 tests pass now. The `renderList` implementation in `src/block.js`:

```js
function renderList(items, definitions) {
  const rendered = items.map((item) => {
    const text = renderInline(item.text, definitions)
    if (item.children.length === 0) return `<li>${text}</li>`
    return `<li>${text}\n${renderList(item.children, definitions)}\n</li>`
  })
  return `<ul>\n${rendered.join('\n')}\n</ul>`
}
```

This matches the spec: an item without children renders as `<li>text</li>` on one line; an item with children renders `<li>`, the item's own text, a newline, the nested `<ul>...</ul>` on its own lines, then `</li>` on its own line — recursing for arbitrarily deep nesting. Only `src/block.js`'s `renderList` body was changed; no other file, export, or function was touched.

